  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Hockey (Canadian fishing game, 1961). 2-player, 52-card deck. Periods: 3 (plus sudden death if tied). Deal: 5 cards per player per deal, 6 in final deal of period. Turn: Play card to pile. Breakaway: Match top card rank OR play Jack. Goal: Opponent matches your card after your breakaway = 1 goal. Scoring: Most goals after 3 periods wins match.',
    Player: "Welcome to Hockey, the Canadian card game that brings ice hockey to your table. Play three periods, each using the full 52-card deck. Create a 'breakaway' by playing a card matching the top pile card or any Jack. Then, if your opponent's next play matches your card, you score a goal! Most goals after three periods wins the match. Shout 'Breakaway!' and 'Goal!' for thematic fun.",
    objective: "Score more 'goals' than your opponent over three periods of play.",
    gameplay: "1. Players alternate playing one card face up to a central pile.\n2. **Breakaway**: You create a breakaway if you play a card of the SAME rank as the card currently on top of the pile, OR if you play any **Jack**.\n3. **Scoring a Goal**: Once you have a breakaway, you score a goal if you match the NEXT card played by your opponent.\n4. **Defense/Saves**: If your opponent creates a breakaway, your current breakaway is cancelled. You can also 'save' a goal attempt by playing a card that your opponent cannot match.",
    keyRules: [
      'Follow the legal action constraints defined for Hockey.',
      'Round outcome is resolved by the scoring method: Scoring summary: Players score goals by creating breakaways and matching opponent cards.',
      "Winning condition: Score more 'goals' than your opponent over three periods of play.",
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: '2 players (opposing teams).',
      deck: 'Standard 52-card deck. No Jokers.',
      equipment: 'Standard 52-card deck. Pencil and paper optional for keeping score.',
      dealing: "A match consists of three 'periods'. In each period, the entire 52-card deck is dealt in batches of 5 cards per player. The final deal of the period is 6 cards each.",
    },
    turnFlow: "1. Players alternate playing one card face up to a central pile.\n2. **Breakaway**: You create a breakaway if you play a card of the SAME rank as the card currently on top of the pile, OR if you play any **Jack**.\n3. **Scoring a Goal**: Once you have a breakaway, you score a goal if you match the NEXT card played by your opponent.\n4. **Defense/Saves**: If your opponent creates a breakaway, your current breakaway is cancelled. You can also 'save' a goal attempt by playing a card that your opponent cannot match.",
